       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Ordered:** metformin 4250 mg PO TID, which is 12,750 mg/day.\n- **Maximum labeled dose:** 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, usually given as 850 mg TID. Many references use 2,000 mg/day. Extended-release is capped at 2,000 mg/day.\n- **Risk:** This is about 5 times the maximum daily dose. It carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nI suspect a typo, and 850 mg or 425 mg may have been intended. Could you confirm the dose you want? Typical options are:\n\n- 850 mg PO TID with meals (2,550 mg/day)\n- 500 mg PO BID or TID with meals\n- 1,000 mg PO BID with meals\n\nPlease also tell me whether you want immediate-release or extended-release. Once you confirm, I'll enter the order right away."
